      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Sinus tenderness has not been quantitatively assessed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "We sought to compare sinus and systemic tenderness in rhinosinusitis, allergic rhinitis, and chronic fatigue syndrome (CFS), and healthy (non-CFS) groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Cutaneous pressures (kg/cm(2)) causing pain at 5 sinus and 18 systemic sites were measured in acute and chronic rhinosinusitis, active allergic rhinitis, healthy non-CFS/no rhinosinusitis, and CFS subjects."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Sinus thresholds differed significantly (P <\/= 10(-11), ANOVA) between non-CFS/no rhinosinusitis (1.59 +/- 0.14 kg/cm(2), mean +/- 95% CI, n = 117), allergic rhinitis (1.19 +/- 0.31, n = 30), exacerbations of chronic rhinosinusitis (1.25 +/- 0.26, n = 25), non-CFS/chronic rhinosinusitis (1.23 +/- 0.27, n = 23), acute rhinosinusitis (1.10 +/- 0.20, n = 22), CFS/no rhinosinusitis (0.98 +/- 0.15, n = 70), and CFS/chronic rhinosinusitis (0.78 +/- 0.12, n = 56). Systemic pressure thresholds were lower for CFS (1.46 +/- 0.15) than for non-CFS (2.67 +/- 0.22, P <\/= 10(-11))."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The lower sinus thresholds of rhinosinusitis groups validated the sign of sinus tenderness. Sinus and systemic thresholds were both 44% lower in CFS than in non-CFS subjects, suggesting that systemic hyperalgesia contributed to CFS sinus tenderness and \"rhinosinusitis\" complaints."
        }
      ]},
